      "message": "I hesitate about a linear fit to this considering we only have 2 datapoints (2.25A and 3A). By this fit, if we had a 1A PD charger, we would set the current limit to 384mA, which seems way too low. And if you charge from another samus (900mA), it will cut the charge rate in half. I vaguely remember testing how much current we draw from another samus with the existing 192mA offset and it was very close to the desired 900mA. So it makes me doubt the linear fit here. I\u0027m not a fan of artificially lowering our charge rate whre it\u0027s not needed, but if you guys have the data to say this is necessary then go ahead.",
